{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f3_tunnelset_epoch_collision", "label": "F3 \u2014 TunnelSet bare-epoch keying collision", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "main.rs:3688-3794, tunnelset.rs:51-53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TunnelSet is keyed by a bare epoch number meaning different things for own-tuns (own epoch) and overlap-tuns (peer's pending epoch); bring_up bails on a duplicate key and the ? aborts the whole peer loop, so neither side forms an overlap and nobody acks."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_initiate_due_rotations_in_step_timer", "label": "initiate_due_rotations rotates every gateway on one global timer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "services/sync.rs:640-688, lib.rs:702", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_jitter_non_mitigation", "label": "Jitter is NOT a mitigation for the epoch collision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The collision is not about simultaneity but about what the epoch key means; once the fabric is in step, staggering only moves when a Role-B bring_up collides with the gateway's own active tun. Corrects the verification's own earlier recommendation."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f2_directive_epoch_mint_mismatch", "label": "F2 \u2014 mint epoch vs directive epoch mismatch wedges the store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "epochkeys.rs:79, main.rs:3680-3692", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After a crash plus re-directive the gateway mints epoch N+1 but proceeds on the directive epoch, so the wire is self-consistent while the store is not; cutover promotes the stale entry and select_boot_key boots a dead key."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f4_orphaned_retiring_key", "label": "F4 \u2014 no boot-time scrub of orphaned retiring epoch keys", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "epoch_keys.json", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The controller grew exactly this cleanup in sweep_rotations step 3; the gateway did not. F4 is 'mirror what the controller already does'."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f8_role_b_active_tun_awareness", "label": "F8 \u2014 Role-B collapse has no active-tun awareness", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f9_role_b_abort_leak", "label": "F9 \u2014 the abort path leaks Role-B overlap state", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "main.rs:3902-3906, main.rs:3765", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "maybe_collapse_role_b only arms when the peer's active key equals the key we overlapped toward; on abort the predicate never matches, so the overlap Device, enforcer entry, routes and wg0_pins entry leak forever and contains_key blocks that peer from ever being overlapped again. Not live today only because abort is reachable solely via rule 2 \u2014 OD-4 makes it live."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_od4_ack_threshold", "label": "OD-4 \u2014 three-tier ack threshold for rule 4", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rule 4 must stay in some form (an offline peer must not block a rotation forever), so the fix is a threshold question, not an inversion: promote at 90s with >=1 live ack or with no expected peers; with expected peers and zero acks wait to a longer deadline then Abort. Needs ack re-delivery and a gateway-side abort transition, neither of which exists."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_t0_pathctx_rotation_overlap_handle", "label": "T0 \u2014 shared PathCtx rotation-overlap handle precursor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three independent verifications found the same missing handle (key-rotation T4, the proto block's cutover hard-skip, the relay mux's channels) \u2014 one Arc field plus an accessor, built once outside all three."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_stub_gateway_epoch_ack_local_endpoints", "label": "StubGateway::report_epoch_acks sends destructive empty local_endpoints", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "testkit/src/lib.rs:1245", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_epoch0_private_key_disk_residual", "label": "Epoch-0 private key survives on disk in two files", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "identity.rs:22,93,95", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forward secrecy on rotation is true for live Devices and epoch_keys.json and false on disk; the legacy fallback is load-bearing for select_boot_key and from_legacy, so it cannot simply be deleted \u2014 file identity-key retirement separately."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_initiate_due_rotations_in_step_timer", "target": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f3_tunnelset_epoch_collision", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f3_tunnelset_epoch_collision", "target": "docs_research_in_step_rotation_cutover_arbitration_fabric_wide_outage_2026_08_31", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_jitter_non_mitigation", "target": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f3_tunnelset_epoch_collision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_f9_role_b_abort_leak", "target": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_od4_ack_threshold", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source_location": "OD-4 makes F9 live", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_key_rotation_plan_verification_od4_ack_threshold", "target": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_e_rule4_promotes_dead_key", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-plan-verification.md", "source